## Risks

!! Chargeback rate is 0.61% against our 0.50% ceiling. Our acquirer opens a formal review at 0.65%, which brings fines starting at $25,000 per month and a remediation plan. At the current trend we cross that line in about two weeks.

data risks = risk,likelihood,impact,owner,mitigation
data risks += Chargebacks cross the 0.65% acquirer threshold,High,"Fines from $25,000 per month plus a remediation plan",Tomas Reyes,"Friendly-fraud rule tuning ships Oct 20; weekly review with Risk"
data risks += EU routing slips past the Nov 1 pilot,Medium,"Pilot (about $2.3M monthly volume) moves to December",Marcus Webb,"Escalated to the acquirer account lead; fallback is the current acquirer at +0.3 pts in fees"
data risks += Ledger v2 not ready for the Oct 30 quarter-end close,Medium,"Finance keeps manual reconciliation, about 12 analyst-hours per week",Samir Patel,"Prioritize the 5 remaining partners by volume; daily check-in"
data risks += Apple Pay coverage gap while Mei is out Oct 26 to 30,Low,"Slower response to wallet incidents",Dana Okafor,"Runbook handoff and a named backup by Oct 23"

